# Write "Genuary". Avoid using a font.

<small>Genuary 2026, day 05 — prompt by Piero</small>

<VideoLoop src="/05/loop.mp4" poster="/05/poster.jpg" label="Wobbly softbody letters spelling GENUARY dropping onto the floor, with confetti" />

No font, so the letters are drawn by hand: in the interactive sketch every click
adds a point, closing the loop turns the points into a soft body — and suddenly
your letterform is jelly fighting for its life under gravity. Same spring-ring
construction as day 02, but here it has to keep seven letters legible while they
fall, bounce and slump into each other. When the word survives, confetti
(200 tiny physics bodies, also not a font).

For the clip above the click-drawn outlines come from tracing tiny 5&times;7
pixel-grid letters, so the render stays reproducible — still no font in sight.

```kotlin
// every softbody: outline points become circles chained with springs
for (i in createdBodies.indices) {
    val nextIndex = (i + 1) % createdBodies.size
    edgeJoints.add(createSpringJoint(world, createdBodies[i], createdBodies[nextIndex],
        frequency = 3f, damping = 0.7f))
}
// plus longer diagonal springs (skip 2, n/3, n/2) so the letter
// wobbles instead of collapsing
```

